positions.description:
Full-time work on Incident Management Mobile app under OutageHub Team (Android/iOS native components).

■ Worked on development CI/CD  infra deploy for a list of critical Service Level Indicators and monitors for a major executive ask to cover our service health in dashboard;
■ Run weekly deployments for services and infra-resources
■ Improved usability, accessibility and performance reducing memory leaks and crashes by 40% in the app for 2,500+ daily users,
■ Developed APIs to fetch object metadata and improve loading time with pagination, reduced loading times by 800ms for outage display;
■ Developed Android Widget for Azure CXP VPs to display list of Top Outages with on-demand and scheduled refresh.

■ Led Crisis Bridge summarization project for Incident Management using Python to generate prompt templates and
processing raw files then using Chat-GPT 4 for summarizing bridge discussion for ~2k daily outage calls;
■ Used .NET to create microservices for IcM using webhook that creates crisis bridge calls and generates the Teams transcripts with service accounts join call to get access to transcripts live and summarize it using microservice;
■ Led a Role Based Access feature for limiting participation in outage, used across the company for +90k users

■ Worked on Etsy core-fulfillment project using PHP and React technologies to improve the user experience and
create a new section of the fulfillment administration page to select shipping methods and track their deliveries;
■ Acquired CI/CD and train deployment capabilities in a monolith based repo environment, shipping 2 features.

■ Acquired major skills to develop and integrate applications with Salesforce CRM, including the Apex language and Lightning Web Components for frontend development;
■ Participated in the security consulting of the Government of Colorado, solved security issues that put the institution's
data at stake; removing the risk of SQL injection in their domains completely.

